# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pharmacy claim — membership verification
#
# "Claim or verify your pharmacy" must confirm that the submitted email really
# belongs to the selected pharmacy before it sends anything. Without one of the
# resolvers below, the lookup returns "unknown" and every claim on an already
# registered pharmacy is refused with HTTP 503 (deliberate fail-safe — an
# unverifiable link must never be treated as permission).
#
# Configure EITHER option 1 (preferred) OR option 2.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Option 1 — a dedicated membership check endpoint.
#   Contract:  POST { "email": "...", "pharmacyId": "..." }  ->  { "linked": true|false }
#   Preferred: it answers one narrow question and needs no admin scope.
#
#   Local:      http://localhost:8000/api/pharmacy-membership/check
#   Production: https://get.zoikomeds.com/api/pharmacy-membership/check
#               (HTTPS and the deployed API only — never localhost in production)
# PHARMACY_MEMBERSHIP_LOOKUP_URL=
# PHARMACY_MEMBERSHIP_LOOKUP_KEY=

# Option 2 — the platform admin API, the same source the Super Admin Users page
# reads (GET {NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL}/admin/users). Requires a service account with
# admin scope. Use a long-lived service token where possible; the email/password
# pair is supported for environments that only issue session logins.
# PLATFORM_SERVICE_TOKEN=
# PLATFORM_SERVICE_EMAIL=
# PLATFORM_SERVICE_PASSWORD=

# Exposes POST /internal/pharmacy-membership/check for operational verification.
# The endpoint is DISABLED unless this is set: it answers "does <email> belong to
# <pharmacy>?", which is an account enumeration oracle if left open.
# PHARMACY_MEMBERSHIP_CHECK_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Platform / backend
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Defaults to https://get.zoikomeds.com/api when unset.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://get.zoikomeds.com/api
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://zoiko-meds-platform.vercel.app

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pharmacy search
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Server-only. Enables geocoding and the Google Places source that finds
# pharmacies not yet on the platform (the "unclaimed" claim path). Without it
# only the ZoikoMeds directory is searched.
# GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Email (SMTP)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SMTP_HOST=
# SMTP_PORT=465
# SMTP_USER=
# SMTP_PASS=
# SMTP_FROM_NAME=
# SMTP_FROM_ADDRESS=
# RECIPIENT_EMAIL=info@zoikomeds.com
